# Deal Radar backend settings. Copy to backend/.env and fill in real values.
# backend/.env is gitignored and must stay that way — never commit a secret.

# ── Microsoft Graph: attachment bytes ────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by POST /api/activity/attachments/fetch-from-graph, which is the only
# way to get an attachment's REAL bytes. The Outlook connector can list what
# came with an email but returns a PDF as text and an image as a picture.
#
# App-only (client credentials), so there is no signed-in user and no "/me".
# The app registration needs the APPLICATION permission Mail.Read with ADMIN
# CONSENT granted. A delegated Mail.Read grant authenticates fine and then
# 403s on every message — that is the most common first-setup failure.
#
# Entra portal → App registrations → your app:
#   GRAPH_CLIENT_ID     Overview → Application (client) ID
#   GRAPH_TENANT_ID     Overview → Directory (tenant) ID
#   GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET Certificates & secrets → the secret VALUE (not its ID;
#                       the value is shown once, when it is created)
#   GRAPH_MAILBOX       the mailbox to read, e.g. jzamer@z-reg.com
#
# This file is a committed TEMPLATE, so it carries no real values — not even
# the client id, which is not secret but does identify the tenant.
GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=
GRAPH_MAILBOX=

# ── Where attachments are filed ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Defaults to <repo>/attachments. The database stores a path
# RELATIVE to this, so moving the folder needs no data change.
# DOCUMENTS_FOLDER=C:\Users\Jackz\CRE-deal-radar-platform\attachments

# Optional. Per-file ceiling in bytes; defaults to 50MB. A file over it is
# recorded and marked oversize, never written, and never fails the entry.
# MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES=52428800

# ── Model keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
